= Cognitive load — Simple =

'''Cognitive load''' is the mental demand a task places on limited processing resources.

[[Working memory/Simple|Working memory]] can only keep and work with a limited amount of information at once.

A task can overload you because the subject itself is complex, or because the instructions and presentation make you do unnecessary mental work.

Cognitive load is not exactly the same as difficulty. Something can be difficult but well organized, or easy material can be made confusing by poor design.

Good teaching tries to remove unnecessary load while keeping the thinking that actually helps learning.

